column2:
Keshava, Madhava, Vishnu, Govinda, Madhusudana, Padmanabha, Hrishikesha, Shridhara and Trivikrama,
skandapuran:34:104	Damodara, Vasudeva and Hari I salute, adorned with conch, discus, mace, Sharnga and the forest garland;
skandapuran:34:105	lord of the worlds, lord of the universe, lord of Shri, most learned of all, beloved of Shri, bearer of Shri, lord of Shri, abode of Shri — I bow to you.
skandapuran:34:106	Achyuta, Ananta, lord of sacrifice, ruler of sacrifice, salutation to you; to you whose form is Rik, Saman and Atharva, to you whose form is sacrifice, salutation;
skandapuran:34:107	salutation to you in the forms of Man-Lion, Fish, Boar and Tortoise; salutation to you mounted on the vehicle of holy places, Garuda-bannered one.
skandapuran:34:108	The thousand-headed god, with parts and without, supreme, the knowable Person, the overseer, the first, Narayana the lord —
skandapuran:34:109	I always bow to the god Hari, destroyer of the daityas, womb of gold, womb of the earth, womb of sacrifice, source of nectar;
skandapuran:34:110	to you, womb of Shri and womb of knowledge, Vasudeva, salutation. By you this whole world, moving and unmoving, was created, lord;
skandapuran:34:111	you are creator, protector and destroyer age after age; with eyes everywhere, unmanifest, to be known, with faces everywhere,
skandapuran:34:112	self of the universe, god everywhere, Vasudeva, salutation to you. You are the sun, the wind, the fire and the moon;
skandapuran:34:113	you are the Creator, lord of gods, you are Indra, you are Prajapati; by your grace, best of gods, my sacrifice was accomplished.
